/T (26. Thailand emphasizes that disruption to essential State functions, absent accompanying physical destruction, injury, or loss of life, does not by itself amount to an armed attack. The invocation of self-defence must strictly comply with the principles of necessity, proportionality, and immediacy, and must be based on responsible and reasonably certain attribution to a State.)
/E (26. Thailand emphasizes that disruption to essential State functions, absent accompanying physical destruction, injury, or loss of life, does not by itself amount to an armed attack. The invocation of self-defence must strictly comply with the principles of necessity, proportionality, and immediacy, and must be based on responsible and reasonably certain attribution to a State.)
