/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (28. The principle of due diligence is firmly established in international law, as recognized by the International Court of Justice \(ICJ\) in the Corfu Channel case \(1949\), where the Court confirmed that a State must not knowingly allow its territory to be used for acts contrary to the rights of other States.)
/E (28. The principle of due diligence is firmly established in international law, as recognized by the International Court of Justice \(ICJ\) in the Corfu Channel case \(1949\), where the Court confirmed that a State must not knowingly allow its territory to be used for acts contrary to the rights of other States.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3 4]
>>
endobj
