/T (34. Accordingly, the foundational principles of distinction, proportionality, military necessity, and humanity must guide the conduct of cyber activities during armed conflicts, as they do for operations in other domains. These principles serve to protect civilian populations, civilian objects, and essential public services from the effects of hostilities.)
/E (34. Accordingly, the foundational principles of distinction, proportionality, military necessity, and humanity must guide the conduct of cyber activities during armed conflicts, as they do for operations in other domains. These principles serve to protect civilian populations, civilian objects, and essential public services from the effects of hostilities.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [0]
>>
