/T (37. Thailand further stresses that applying International Humanitarian Law to the use of ICTs in the context of armed conflicts does not in any way encourage or legitimize conflict. IHL regulates the conduct of hostilities with the sole aim of limiting human suffering and protecting those not participating in hostilities, without affecting the legality of the use of force under the Charter of the United Nations.)
/E (37. Thailand further stresses that applying International Humanitarian Law to the use of ICTs in the context of armed conflicts does not in any way encourage or legitimize conflict. IHL regulates the conduct of hostilities with the sole aim of limiting human suffering and protecting those not participating in hostilities, without affecting the legality of the use of force under the Charter of the United Nations.)
